A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
ZIF - CLEAR ALL CONDITIONAL LEVELS

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    ZIF

Clears every active IF level, even if the current state is false. Use
deliberately to recover from an unfinished conditional sequence.

It can make following commands execute that would otherwise have been
skipped. In scripts, prefer correctly matched IF/ELSE/FI rather than
relying on global cleanup.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
